+**Data Structures:**
+The SVO is implemented as a template class `tree<FORMAT_T, BIT_WIDTH, DETAILS>` [S1, unofficial].
+1.  **`node_format`**: Stores node metadata.
+    *   `_depth`: `uint32_t`, the current depth in the tree.
+    *   `_mask`: Bitmask indicating which of the 8 children exist.
+    *   `_block_index`: Index into the memory pool's block array.
+2.  **`mem_pool<T>`**: Manages fixed-size blocks of memory.
+    *   `_blocks`: Array of `T[]` (blocks).
+    *   `_free`: Free list for block reuse.
+    *   Block capacity is fixed at 8 elements per block [S1, unofficial].
+3.  **`_root_node`**: The root of the tree, initialized with `_depth=0` and an allocated node block [S1, unofficial].
+4.  **`_node_pool`**: Memory pool for `node_format` instances.
+5.  **`_voxel_pool`**: Memory pool for `FORMAT_T` (voxel data) instances.
+
+**Parameters:**
+*   `BIT_WIDTH`: Template parameter for coordinate precision. Values are 16 or 32 [S1, unofficial].
+*   `MAX_DEPTH`: Derived from `BIT_WIDTH`. For 16-bit, `MAX_DEPTH=5` ($32^3$ space); for 32-bit, `MAX_DEPTH=10` ($1024^3$ space) [S1, unofficial].
+*   `AXIS_WIDTH`: $2^{MAX\_DEPTH}$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   `BOUNDS[3]`: Maximum bounds per axis. Defaults to `AXIS_WIDTH` if not specified [S1, unofficial].
+*   `_discard_overflow`: Boolean flag. If `true`, out-of-bounds voxels are silently dropped; if `false`, an assertion triggers [S1, unofficial].
